# Generated review artifacts. panel.py writes one per commit sha, so the file count
# moves on every commit, and docs/CODEBASE-MAP.md records a count per directory. The
# result was that a green gate turned codemap red on its own next run, which cost four
# regenerate-commit cycles on 2026-08-05 before the mechanism was named. gate.py already
# treats this directory as its own exhaust (GATE_OUTPUTS, gate.py:204) and CI regenerates
# the artifact for the exact commit it is testing (ship-gate.yml:116), so nothing needs
# the committed copy.
state/reviews/*.json

# Extracted commercial book text, added 2026-08-09. 150 files, 8 MB, full chapter
# bodies from published works (Software Engineering at Google and others). The
# global knowledge rule is that commercial books are metadata-only unless private
# extraction rights are explicitly attested, and are never redistributed or
# reconstructed. Committing full text to a repository is reconstruction, so the
# corpus stays on disk, readable just in time, and out of git history where it
# could not be removed later without a rewrite.
docs/books/

# An inbox of another repository's docs, dropped here for reading, not for tracking.
# Swept in by a git add -A on 2026-08-10 and it carried a live secret. It stays on
# disk and out of the index; see docs/analysis/2026-08-10-inbox-secret-exposure.md.
docs/inbox-from-new-recruit/
*:Zone.Identifier

# Reanimation corpora are private family/friend messages, never committed
.intent/
